{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And he took the stone.</b> It is the Foundation Stone, from which the world was founded." "<b>And he poured oil on its top.</b> He anointed it to consecrate it, to offer sacrifices upon it when he returns from Paddan-aram. As we find with the vessels of the Tabernacle: 'and you shall anoint them and consecrate them.' And so it is proven right before us: 'I am El of Beth El, where you anointed a pillar to Me.' Another interpretation: he anointed it as a sign, so that he would recognize it when he returns."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:06:29.544111273Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}